WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.820
This fourth of July, when you

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.120
watch the fireworks

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.560
will you think about

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.580
this?

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.680
The Declaration of Independence?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.460
We should.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.900
After all, the holiday's meant to honor this,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.480
not just fireworks.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.980
Though, those are nice.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.779
Although it's ironic that since

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:19.839
America's founding,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.920
government has grown so much

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.720
that you may not be allowed to buy fireworks

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:24.997
where you live.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.413
All these places ban them

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.580
in the name of safety,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.740
The Declaration

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.220
isn't about safety

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.120
or things government should do

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.000
it's about limiting government,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.600
it's about freedom.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.460
The founders were sick of British oppression.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.040
They worried about government having

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.080
too much power.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.920
Thomas Jefferson and his colleagues

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.159
wrote the Declaration

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.220
to create a new form of government,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.840
one where people could rule themselves.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.860
It worked.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.540
When the Declaration was signed,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.220
America was considered a backwater.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.900
But very few years later, America was the

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.285
most prosperous and

00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:04.380
probably the freest country in the world.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.120
The fourth of July celebrates the Declaration,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.700
which led to the Constitution,

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.180
the document that really

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.060
lays out the rules

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.720
meant to limit government.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.500
"Trust no man with too much power",

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.860
said Jefferson

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.300
"bind them with the chains of the Constitution."

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.320
It's chains

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.880
have done a lot of good.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.120
We have a right not to have our home searched

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.360
without a warrant,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.740
a right to bear arms,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.260
to free speech.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.320
It's good we declared

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.312
independence from Britain

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.920
because in Britain, government sentenced this man

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.580
to more than a year in jail

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.820
"I've caused a breach of peace.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.640
I'm being arrested"

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.120
for making this Facebook live video

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.360
outside a courthouse.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.900
Others get locked up for things they write.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.980
Hundreds get arrested every year.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.160
Sentenced for writing an offending comment.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.259
Fortunately in America, thanks to

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.220
the Constitution, we can say most anything we want

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.720
without being jailed.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.974
We also have a right to bear arms,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.240
but the country we rebelled against has

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.500
some of the strictest gun regulations in the world.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.960
Those regulations haven't stopped crime.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.900
So now they're going after people who have knives.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.540
One British police agency bragged

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.480
about a weapon sweep

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.320
that found scissors and pliers.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.480
But don't worry, they've been taken off the streets.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.340
I'm glad I live in America

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.240
where I can carry pliers

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.600
and speak freely.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.680
And there's more to the Constitution

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.400
than the First and Second Amendments.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.600
Supreme Court overruled.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.100
The Supreme Court overruled.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.260
Supreme Court overruled.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.280
The Constitution divided government power

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.220
in ways that limit

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.770
authoritarian politicians from both

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.520
parties.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.500
We are throwing them the hell out of our country.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.640
Trump's own appointee ruled that a law

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.920
making it easier to deport some immigrants

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.340
was too vague.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.580
Allow intelligence agencies to track

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.830
who a terrorist is in contact with.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.798
The Supreme Court stopped

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.300
the Obama administration a hundred times.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.900
No President Obama,

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.360
the Fourth Amendment says government

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.940
cannot just search people's cell phones.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.080
They have to get a search warrant.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.430
No, you can't just declare

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.720
carbon dioxide to be a pollutant.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.650
A major setback tonight for President Obama's

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.280
climate change initiative.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.080
I'm glad we have this document.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.380
It has often kept presidents and Congress

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.920
and judges from grabbing too much power.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.320
The limits stated in here

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.300
have not fully succeeded,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.032
unfortunately.

00:03:29.032 --> 00:03:30.340
Thomas Jefferson promised

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.960
"a wise and frugal government."

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:33.860
Frugal?

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.840
Give me a break!

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.500
We're already more than 21

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.240
trillion dollars in debt.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.410
Jefferson also wrote about leaving men "free to regulate

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.000
their own pursuits."

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.580
Now we've got more than 180,000 pages of rules.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.480
Still, the

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.240
Constitution and the Declaration of Independence

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.920
have helped keep us free.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.340
That's something

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.780
to celebrate.

